/-! ### Round 66 (2026-05-15) — corner case: $A_0 = \{2, 4, 5, 7, 8\}$,
    $A_1 = \{3, 6\}$, $A_2 = \{1\}$.

  The case where $\chi(9) = \chi(18)$ (= color 1), so Round 65's
  argument doesn't apply ($c_1 = c_2$ in AP5_no_partition).

  Different attack: chain of mono-triple deductions.
  1. $\chi(2) \ne 0$ (via $C_0$) and $\chi(2) \ne 2$ (mono $(3, 2,
     3)$ if $\chi(2) = 2$): $\chi(2) = 1$.
  2. $\chi(4) \ne 0$ (via $C_0$) and $\chi(4) \ne 2$ (mono $(3, 3,
     4)$): $\chi(4) = 1$.
  3. $\chi(8) \ne 0$, $\chi(8) \ne 1$ (mono $(18, 2, 8)$ with
     $\chi(2) = 1$): $\chi(8) = 2$.
  4. $\chi(7) \ne 0$, $\chi(7) \ne 1$ (mono $(9, 4, 7)$ with
     $\chi(4) = 1$): $\chi(7) = 2$.
