  Proof: self-loop Rado triple $(9, 6, 9)$ satisfies $9 + 3 \cdot
  6 = 27 = 3 \cdot 9$; monochromaticity requires $\chi(9) =
  \chi(6) = \chi(9)$, i.e., $\chi(9) = \chi(6)$.

  This is a UNIVERSAL fact about Rado-mono-free 3-colorings —
  independent of any specific configuration on multiples of 3.
